  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 602588316}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0fb95ba1b6960e3458f1995e5c414a9f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Level
  TutorialText: 'In this level we''ll learn that code can be repeated!


    <u><i>Loops</i></u>

    Loops
    is any block of code that repeats itself using some logic.

    We''ll see loops
    that go from one number up to some number and then another loop that goes through
    a list of items.

    For now imagine the list of items as a person listing you
    his favorite shows.


    <u><i>Conditions/If statements</i></u>

    Conditions
    are used to run some code <i>if</i> the checked value or variable is equal to
    true.

    Otherwise, if false, the code will not run. They are perfect to run
    some logic only in some condition!


    <u><i>Sending data from terminal to
    terminal</i></u>

    We''ll see that you can send data from one terminal to
    another.


    Have fun!'
  OnTutorialFinishEvent:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
